<title>USA: Sigma Circuits Inc Q3 March 31 shr loss.</title>
<headline>Sigma Circuits Inc Q3 March 31 shr loss.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 Mos ended 3/31  9 Mos ended 3/31</p>
<p>				    1997	  1996    1997     1996</p>
<p> Net sales		    $20,425    $24,330 $59,143  $67,117</p>
<p> Cost of sales		 17,911     19,394  50,775   52,736</p>
<p> Gross profit		   2,514	4,936   8,368   14,381</p>
<p> SG&amp;A			     4,186	2,616   8,795    8,275</p>
<p> Amortization of goodwill     125	  157     376	364</p>
<p> Facility closing costs	  --	   --   (250)	 --</p>
<p> Operating income (loss)  (1,797)	2,163   (553)    5,742</p>
<p> Interest expense, net	  479	  497   1,531    1,171</p>
<p>Income (loss) before</p>
<p>  income taxes		(2,276)	1,666  (2,084)   4,571</p>
<p>Provision (benefit) for</p>
<p>  income taxes		  (541)	  546   (439)    1,736</p>
<p> Net income (loss)	  (1,735)	1,120 (1,645)  (2,835)</p>
<p> Net EPS (loss)		(0.43)	 0.23  (0.41)     0.62</p>
<p> Shrs			    4,074	4,845   4,030    4,587</p>
<p>			(In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: 1997 Q3 includes a $1.5 million one-time charge to operations related to receivables, inventory, and other costs associated with one customer.  Additionally, the Company charged $1.2 million to operations primarily for obsolete inventory and equipment and an unfavorable sales tax ruling.  </p>
<p>The $2.7 million of pre-tax charges hurt earnings per share by $.48.</p>
<p>For the nine months period, results include $3.4 million of pre-tax charges which hurt share results by $0.57 on an after-tax basis.</p>
</text>
